<h2>Engineering trade-offs and validation</h2>
<p>Building on ERPNext preserves a shared transactional foundation, but it makes integration testing important. I separate interface feedback from server validation, keep loading and failure states explicit, and use role-aware controls without relying on navigation visibility for authorization.</p>
<p>Backend tests and Playwright interface tests support the development process. Testing software behavior is distinct from confirming deployment, data quality and day-to-day operational use. This portfolio does not present historical project tests as a fresh production acceptance run.</p>

<h2>Current status</h2>
<p>REVE ONE is application-development and staged-integration work. Production deployment and factory-wide adoption are not independently established, so I do not describe it as a fully operational factory system. The public overview intentionally omits internal rollout records and compatibility findings.</p>
